    "issue_description": "> **OMAC 控制的执行。第一动作必须严格执行：**\n\n```bash\nOMAC_ENGINE=multica OMAC_WORKSPACE_ID=410ade5e-8ae0-4402-b975-813dea2ff3e1 OMAC_PROJECT_ID=732ce83f-5cbd-4485-850d-1b8a1bf16340 omac work show 01a0fb38-0558-7ae0-a2b1-23b00e56190a --output json\n```\n\n> `omac work show` 和 `omac work submit` 都可能长时间运行。任何工具调用在拿到最终 tool_result 和终态退出码前都不完整。若工具返回 running/session、缺少最终 tool_result、出现空输出或不完整输出，必须等待或轮询到终态。使用足够长的 wait/yield，或保留并恢复续接句柄；这是通用终态规则，不绑定某个具体工具 API。timeout/yield 不是空结果，也不允许据此停止。`omac work show` 只有在退出码 0 且得到可解析 JSON 后才能继续。`omac work submit` 只有在最终 tool_result 明确给出退出码 0，且 JSON 包含 `\"ok\": true`、`\"terminal\": true` 和 `\"next_action\": \"stop\"` 时才可宣称成功。结果未知时不得宣称成功或结束；validation error 必须修复后重新提交。submit 成功就是本次执行的最后动作，立即停止，不再执行任何平台写入。\n\n> 在上方精确的 `omac work show` 命令以退出码 0 成功返回可解析 JSON 前，不得执行任何其他 Issue 查询（包括 `multica issue get`、`multica issue comment list` 或 metadata 查询），也不得开始分析任务内容。work show 成功后，只能在返回上下文确有需要时使用只读 Issue 查询。禁止任何会创建、修改或删除 Issue 状态的 `multica issue` 写操作。这是语义边界，不是穷举命令清单；禁止示例包括 `multica issue status`、`multica issue assign`、`multica issue comment`、`multica issue metadata`、`multica issue rerun`、`multica issue cancel-task`、`multica issue update`、`multica issue create`、`multica issue label`、`multica issue property`、`multica issue reorder` 和 `multica issue subscriber`。只允许使用上方给出的精确 `omac work show` 命令，以及 work show 返回的精确 `omac work submit` 命令作为 OMAC 控制命令；已有手工附件或 verification 但缺少 `delivery_identity` 时也必须通过该 submit 命令封存。\n\n# Repair Harness SDK production compilation without changing behavior\n\n## 任务摘要\n- 类型: 开发实现（`develop`）\n- 执行角色: 开发执行者（`worker`）\n- 目标: Restore the production build of the existing public Harness SDK by removing the test-only operationPointer dependency from measuredRecoveryMatrixForExecutor at sdk/harness/conformance.go:1402, without changing any public API, runtime or conformance behavior. Preserve the existing caller-constructed Unknown observation and ErrRetryNotPermitted check; construct the same ordinary ExternalOperation data (SystemType fixture, ExternalID external-1) in the production compilation unit at that call site rather than importing/moving test authority or adding a new public helper. This is a compensating owner repair, not a reopening of completed harness-sdk or a new implementation of the SDK.\nRun all inherited SDK verification commands in their original order and every inherited SDK gate unchanged on the committed repair revision; then prove both standalone SDK and full-repository production builds and uncached full tests. Preserve the SDK85 raw unfiltered gate, all fixed 50 required tests, 13 measured semantic rows, seven current-amendment rows, 15 service cases and four receipt-tree regressions. Do not use compilation or negative-only conformance as Host-positive authority. Whole-SDK90 and Host90 remain mandatory in the unchanged downstream Host gates, not falsely claimed as completed here.\nPublish a new immutable source-bound repair evidence set under harness-sdk-build-repair-evidence, including the existing SDK gate artifacts, coverage-audit.md, coverage-block-audit.md, source-snapshot.md and an owner-repair.md. The owner-repair record must bind the exact before/after source and toolchain, failed production build before repair, passing builds after repair, SDK profile raw covered/total statements, all actual command exits, the narrow diff, and compatibility/security review. Regenerate receipt-tree-design-evidence.md for the repaired source, documenting that the shared measurement/seal algorithm itself is unchanged; no historical proof is rewritten or reused as fresh. Use the existing packaging owner/component harness-sdk and sdk/harness source selection; a new DAG task ID does not create a new release component or change the ownership catalog. Source bundle, semantic evidence and verification must bind to the same committed repair source revision and submitted PR HEAD. Preserve old harness-sdk artifacts as historical evidence, never overwrite their immutable delivery.\nThe owner continues existing independent PR90 to main; do not create a duplicate repair PR. Reviewer must reproduce the production build and existing gates, inspect the no-authority/no-API/no-behavior diff, and confirm all required artifact bytes are retrievable. A reviewed merged repair and a buildable main are prerequisites to Audit authoring; a proposed patch or local pass is not enough. If this cannot be achieved inside this exact compile-only boundary, use the current owner-decision blocker protocol with concrete source evidence; do not choose a new API, security policy, coverage relaxation or unrelated repair.\n\nAfter release-preview-audit-vocabulary-repair is independently reviewed and merged to main, preserve and rebase the one-line PR90 repair (e8b8dfb6430208e4bd32c8134dbb6c19f24ad566) onto that merged prerequisite using the same issue and PR, retaining the compile-only SDK diff. Read the exact new Preview owner evidence and regenerate every SDK and repair artifact at the final committed PR HEAD; old PR90 evidence is historical, not current verification. Execute all 23 original verification_commands, in their original order and unchanged, on a native Linux worker with /proc/self/fd available and the actual module-pinned Go 1.26.0 toolchain. The independently reproduced recipe is Linux aarch64 / GOOS=linux / GOARCH=arm64, Go go1.26.0, GCC 13.3.0, empty GOFLAGS, default CGO_ENABLED=0; original command 4 explicitly uses CGO_ENABLED=1 for the race detector. Preflight uname -sm, go version, go env GOOS GOARCH GOVERSION CGO_ENABLED GOFLAGS GOTOOLCHAIN and cc --version; verify native execution, not cross-compilation, wrappers, skipped tests or package filtering. A native Linux full-test pass for the filesystem package only establishes supported descriptor identity inspection plus the existing typed mutation denial: Supported/Supports remain false; no identity-atomic mutation capability is newly claimed. No cluster, namespace, live credential or live fault-injection access is needed or authorized. Record the real environment in env_setup and fresh verification. If this environment cannot be reproduced, use the existing owner-decision stop protocol;

